  "notes": "The D-major 3/4 Beethoven German Dance is WoO 13 No. 1, not WoO 8 No. 1 (WoO 8 No. 1 is in C major), so the title metadata is wrong. Source: Beethoven-Haus Bonn scan of the first edition (Edition Strache No. 24, ed. O. E. Deutsch, 1929), page 6, read from the image. Dance without trio, both repeats written out = 32 bars. Pickup A3 (1 beat); pickup A5 before part 2; final bar 2 beats. The old repo tune was not this dance. LH: D3-F#3-A3 quarter chords (D3-G3-A3 in bars 5 and 7); in part 2, A3 followed by broken-chord eighths (G4/E4 and F#4/D4), then a D4-A3-F#3 unison cadence. Simplified: the last LH G4 eighth in bars 9 and 13 is left out because it sounds together with RH G#4 (minor second). Final D4/D3 held for 2 beats. Validation exceptions (intermediate): D6 in bar 12, and LH G4/F#4 above the LH range; both are the composer's."
